## Animation cookbook

| Animation | Tool | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Flip | Reanimated `rotateY` 0→180 with `perspective` on parent; swap face at 90° | One shared value, derived `frontOpacity`/`backOpacity` |
| Deal (deck → hand slot) | Reanimated `withTiming` on translate + bezier easing | Stagger via `withDelay(index * 80, ...)` |
| Drag-to-swap | `Gesture.Pan()` → shared values → snap to nearest slot on release | Use `withSpring` for snap |
| Discard | `withSequence(scale↓, translateY↑, opacity→0)` | |
| Invalid-move shake | `withSequence(translateX +6, -6, +6, 0)` | 4 keyframes, total ~250ms |
| Reveal sweep (end of round) | Stagger flips left-to-right | One shared value per row, derived per card |

## Performance discipline

- A typical round shows ≤24 cards. Skia handles this easily, but avoid re-rendering all of them on every state change — memoize on `(card.id, faceUp, theme.id)`.
- For drag, the dragging card should re-parent into an overlay layer so its z-index isn't fighting the grid.
- Do not allocate Skia paths inside render — build them once via `useMemo` keyed on the theme.
